error: `run` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  `run` waits for another program to end
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_process_async.sg:3:14
 3 |     try list.run()
   |              ^^^
  hint: `await list.runAsync()` does the same work without holding the thread
